{"title":"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem I4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The larger circle has radius 12 cm. Each of the six identical smaller circles\ntouches its two neighbours and the larger circle. What is the radius of the\nsmaller circle?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/3/6e3d06c0755130a0ee8410321e24b4f90f9aabd9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.5cm); draw((0,3)..(3,0)..(0,-3)..(-3,0)..cycle); for (int i=0;i&lt;6;i=i+1){ draw(dir(60*i)..3*dir(60*i)..cycle); } [/asy]\" width=\"145\" height=\"145\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/b/e8b52e4bb60df8603b471083d289883445019a63.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.5cm); draw((0,3)..(3,0)..(0,-3)..(-3,0)..cycle); for (int i=0;i&lt;6;i=i+1){ draw(dir(60*i)..3*dir(60*i)..cycle); } draw((0,1)..(0,-1)..cycle,rgb(1,0,0)); [/asy]\" width=\"145\" height=\"145\" />\nAdding a circle in the middle makes the solution obvious. Since the radius of the big circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cm, then the diameter of the big circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cm. But this is also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of the little circle's diameter! Therefore, the diameter of the little circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0875b77e90651d0fa5683f72d52c854cdb54be08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24\\div3=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> cm and the radius is therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/3/4f32550f1b3be2504d86c870bde0353a1012648f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{4 \\text{cm}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC\" title=\"2005 PMWC\">2005 PMWC </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I3\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem I3\">Problem I3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I5\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem I5\">Problem I5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\